{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For your seed shall be a ger.</b> In the holy language a man who has a family is called [by analogy to] a branch attached to its root; therefore an ezrach is so called, for its meaning is like \"a flourishing native tree\" (Psalms 37:35). And the meaning of ger is like the gargir (grain), which is cut off from the branch. There are foolish ones for whom this explanation is far-fetched. If they knew the meaning of every letter and its form, they would recognize the truth." "<b>Four hundred years.</b> Until the end of this appointed time, from this day."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:41.518292217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}